You have too few HPs for the first ascension, I'd say. Be very careful!
I'd first of all bless the stack of diluted potions of extra healing and
quaff them all.

>  Amulets
>  u - an uncursed amulet of reflection (being worn)
>  J - the cursed Amulet of Yendor named real
>  Weapons

The Magicbane (currently in your bag) in your hand would have absorbed
quite all of the random curses you suffer from. You can also get Expert
in daggers, BTW.

>  E - 17 blessed +0 arrows (in quiver)
>  F - the cursed rustproof +6 Mjollnir (weapon in hand)

Mjollnir is not the best weapon, especially not for the Plane of Air.
(I'd probably have enchanted Stormbringer, if your skill had become
unrestricted in broadswords.)

>  U - the blessed +6 Longbow of Diana (alternate weapon; not wielded)
>  Armor
>  [...]

Armor is okay.

> [...]
>  Rings
>  d - an uncursed +1 ring of increase damage (on left hand)
>  f - an uncursed ring of levitation

Necessary for Plane of Air and also helpful on Plane of Fire (or on
Plane of Water, if you feel the need to use it there as well).

> M - a blessed +3 ring of protection (on right hand)
> Wands
> n - a wand of death (0:7)

Good for the Wizard and for two of the Riders on Astral level.

> Tools
> a - an uncursed bag of holding <--Empty
> c - an uncursed bag of holding <--Also empty

Drop both bags ASAP.

> [...]
> 
> Contents of the blessed bag of holding:

You have not very much potions of full healing; they might suffice, but
be careful, especially on the Plane of Air.

To detect the portals quickly you should have two more scrolls of gold
detection and some means to confuse yourself.

You're carrying a lot of junk; get rid of amnesia, punishment, destroy
armor, etc. You don't need that many blank scrolls anyway.

I'd prefer the ring of free action (instead of protection).

You should dilute some more of the useless potions to create water, then
increase your stack of holy water by dipping the stack of plain water
into one potion of holy water. One or two blessed scrolls of remove curse
would be handy.

>  [...]

Beyond that I'd say you have quite everything that's necessary.

Good luck!

